  "result": " (https://labchem-wako.fujifilm.com/us/catalog/pdf/catalog_0005.pdf)\nciteturn30view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 weeks ago; Content type: application/pdf; Number of pages: 40; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://labchem-wako.fujifilm.com/us/catalog/pdf/catalog_0005.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 3362\nL0@P0: Food Safety\nL1@P0: Foodborne Pathogens\nL2@P0: Food Allergens\nL3@P0: Mycotoxins\nL4@P0: Pesticide Residue Analysis\nL5@P0: Food Components and Additives\nL6@P0-1: Genetic Testing2\nL7@P1: Food Safety\nL8@P1: Foodborne pathogens are an important issue for\nL9@P1: food manufacturers.\nL10@P1: Example of foodborne pathogen management among food manufacturers.\nL11@P1: 1. Decreasing the risk of food poisoning by combining tests for viable bacteria counts and the detection of food\nL12@P1: poisoning bacteria.\nL13@P1: 2. Rapidity and simplicity are key features for microbial tests adopted for the voluntary hygiene management of food\nL14@P1: processing factories.\nL15@P1: Food allergy is an important issue for food manufacturers.\nL16@P1: Example of food allergen management among food manufacturers.\nL17@P1: 1. Allergen advisory labeling: for allergenic ingredients, for possibility of cross contamination, etc.\nL18@P1: 2. Control of contamination: avoid contamination during processing.\nL19@P1: *Cross contamination may occur during transport and storage of ingredients, manufacturing and processing, and\nL20@P1: packing of products.\nL21@P1: Mycotoxins is an important issue for food manufacturers.\nL22@P1: Example of Mycotoxins management among food manufacturers.\nL23@P1: 1. Mycotoxins are heat stable and thermal treatment during processing and preparation of foods cannot inactivate\nL24@P1: them. Appropriate risk management is required in each step of food supply chain (production and storage of\nL25@P1: field crops, processing, distribution, and consumption).\nL26@P1: 2. Aflatoxins are most toxic of all known mycotoxins and have carcinogenic effect on animals.\nL27@P1: Various regulatory bodies (Codex, EC, US FDA, MHLW of Japan etc.) have set their regulatory limit for aflatoxins.\nL28@P1: NH Foods Ltd. Research and Development Center\nL29@P1: Research to Ensure Food Safety and Security\nL30@P1: One of the missions of the NH Foods Ltd. R&D center is to ensure food safety. The R&D center has innovated food\nL31@P1: safety testing techniques based on immunotechnologies. Leveraging its food allergen test kit, it offers a variety of\nL32@P1: food test kits, including test kits for foodborne pathogens. Their performance has earned strong public recognition.\nL33@P1: They include a food allergen detection kit that complies with the guidelines of the Consumer Affairs Agency of\nL34@P1: Japan. Other examples are mycotoxin detection kit that complies with a notice from Ministry of Heath, Labour and\nL35@P1-2: Welfare of Japan, and verotoxin test kit that is listed in another notice.3\nL36@P2: NH Foods Ltd. Products\nL37@P2: Foodborne pathogen test kits\nL38@P2: by Immuno detection\nL39@P2: “NH Immunochromato”\nL40@P2: The ‘NH Immunochromato’ is a line of testing kits for easy detection of food poisoning bacteria\nL41@P2: and toxins in food products. These are used to increase the level of safety in factory produced\nL42@P2: food items and production lines.\nL43@P2: ‘NH Immunochromato O157’ has been certified as a Performance Tested MethodSM (PTM) by\nL44@P2: the AOAC Research Institute.\nL45@P2: NH Immunochromato includes 8 kits designed for 7 food poisoning bacteria or verotoxin; E. coli\nL46@P2: O157, E. coli O26, E. coli O111, E. coli O103, verotoxin (VT1/2), Listeria, Campylobacter and\nL47@P2: Salmonella.\nL48@P2: O26, O111, and O103: The only commercially available immunochrmatographic assay kits\nL49@P2: Verotoxin 1 & 2: Listed in the notice from the Ministry of Health, Labour and Welfare of Japan\nL50@P2: O26\nL51@P2: Salmonella\nL52@P2: O157\nL53@P2: AOAC-PTM\nL54@P2: O103\nL55@P2: Campylobacter\nL56@P2: O111\nL57@P2: Listeria\nL58@P2-3: Verotoxin 1 & 24\nL59@P3: NH Foods Ltd. Products\nL60@P3: Foodborne pathogen test kits\nL61@P3: NH Immunochromato • Simple and rapid immunochromatographic assays\nL62@P3: • One-step assay: Apply enriched samples to test strips\nL63@P3: • Results in just 15 minutes\nL64@P3: • O26, O111, and O103: The only commercially available Immunochromatographic assay kits in\nL65@P3: the world\nL66@P3: • Used widely in Japan.\nL67@P3: Principle of assay\nL68@P3: 1. When a sample solution is applied to the sample application zone of the test\nL69@P3: strip, it is wicked through reagent zone.\nL70@P3: 2. Target pathogen/toxin (1) in the sample binds to the colloidal gold-labeled\nL71@P3: antibody (2) in the reagent zone.\nL72@P3: 3. The pathogen-antibody complex flows through the nitrocellulose membrane\nL73@P3: which contains a zone of antibody specific to target pathogen/toxin.\nL74@P3: 4. The immune complex is captured and concentrated in the zone (test zone) (3),\nL75@P3: eventually forms a reddish purple line.\nL76@P3: 5. The membrane also contains a control zone where the gold-labeled antibody is\nL77@P3: captured.\nL78@P3: 6. The control line forms in the control zone (4) regardless of the presence of\nL79@P3: target pathogen/toxin in the sample solution. The control line ensures the test is\nL80@P3: working correctly.\nL81@P3: Kit contents\nL82@P3: A : Test strip 2 tests ×10 packs\nL83@P3: B : Instruction manual 1\nL84@P3: C : Plastic bag with zipper 1\nL85@P3: Additionally required materials and instruments\nL86@P3: 1. Enrichment broth\nL87@P3: 2. Stomacher and stomacher bags (preferably with a filter)\nL88@P3: 3. Autoclave\nL89@P3: 4. Incubator\nL90@P3: 5. Balance (capable of weighing 25 g)\nL91@P3: 6. Disposable plastic transfer pipettes and/or appropriate micro pipettes and disposable tips\nL92@P3: 7. Timer\nL93@P3: 8. Disposable polypropylene tubes for sterilization of samples (optional)\nL94@P3: Storage and expiration date\nL95@P3: 1) Storage: Store at 2–8˚C under protection from the light. Avoid freezing.\nL96@P3-4: 2) Expiration date: 12 months from the date of manufacture.5\nL97@P4: NH Foods Ltd. Products\nL98@P4: Comparing operational procedure with culture method (Detection of E.coli O157)\nL99@P4: Test procedures (Detection of E.coli O157)\nL100@P4: NH Immunochromato\nL101@P4: Product Analytes Storage Package Size Wako Cat. No.\nL102@P4: NH Immunochromato O157 *AOAC-RI PTM E. coli O157 2-10˚C 20 tests 304-31361\nL103@P4: NH Immunochromato O26 *The only IC assay kit in the world E. coli O26 2-10˚C 20 tests 304-34421\nL104@P4: NH Immunochromato O111 *The only IC assay kit in the world E. coli O111 2-10˚C 20 tests 301-34431\nL105@P4: NH Immunochromato O103 *The only IC assay kit in the world E. coli O103 2-10˚C 20 tests 382-03971\nL106@P4: NH Immunochromato VT1/2 Verotoxin 1 and verotoxin 2 2-10˚C 20 tests 302-93321\nL107@P4: NH Immunochromato Salmonella Salmonella Enteritidis 2-10˚C 20 tests 303-31691\nL108@P4: NH Immunochromato Listeria Listeria species 2-10˚C 20 tests 300-31581\nL109@P4: NH Immunochromato Campylobacter Campylobacter jejuni and C. coli 2-10˚C 20 tests 301-83141\nL110@P4: Related Products\nL111@P4: Product Storage Package Size Wako Cat. No.\nL112@P4: Polymyxin B Sulfate 2-10˚C 1 g\nL113@P4: 5 g\nL114@P4: 167-11691\nL115@P4: 163-11693\nL116@P4: Day 1\nL117@P4: Day 2\nL118@P4: Sample\nL119@P4: Preparation\nL120@P4: Sample\nL121@P4: Enrichment\nL122@P4: Plating on selective\nL123@P4: isolation medium\nL124@P4: Apply the enriched\nL125@P4: sample to\nL126@P4: the test strip Confirmation tests for\nL127@P4: presumptive positive samples\nL128@P4: Observe test results\nL129@P4: Immunochromatographic assay\nL130@P4: Culture Method\nL131@P4: Day 3\nL132@P4: Observing selective isolation medium.\nL133@P4: Inoculate to characterization medium.\nL134@P4: Day 4\nL135@P4: Observing characterization medium.\nL136@P4: Serotyping.\nL137@P4: Test for verotoxin production.\nL138@P4: Step 1: Sample enrichment\nL139@P4: Step 2: Application to test strip\nL140@P4: Step 3: Observation of the test results\nL141@P4: Add enrichment broth to weighed food sample and homogenize. Incubate the homogenized sample at 42˚C for 18-24 hours.\nL142@P4: Read the test result after 15 minutes.\nL143@P4: Test line Control line\nL144@P4: Procedure A:\nL145@P4: Place a test strip on flat surface and apply 100 µL of the enriched sample\nL146@P4: to the sample application zone.\nL147@P4: Procedure B:\nL148@P4: Transfer 150 µL of the enriched sample into a test tube.\nL149@P4: Put a test strip in the test tube immersing the sample application zone in the sample.\nL150@P4: Positive results: Reddish purple lines appear in the test zone and the control zone in 15 minutes after\nL151@P4: application of sample solutions.\nL152@P4: Negative results: A reddish purple line appears in the control zone.\nL153@P4-5: *Invalid results: No reddish purple line appears in the control zone.O26 O157 O111\nL154@P5: 6\nL155@P5: NH Foods Ltd. Products\nL156@P5: Magnetic beads for Immunomagnetic Separation of Foodborne Pathogens\nL157@P5: NH Beads\nL158@P5: • These kits are designed to separate the target organism rapidly.\nL159@P5: • Small volume (25 tests) ensures minimal wastage during use.\nL160@P5: • Target organism at 102 CFU/mL in solution can be separated.\nL161@P5: NH Beads\nL162@P5: Product Storage Package Size Wako Cat. No.\nL163@P5: NH Beads O157 2-10˚C 20 tests 300-85671\nL164@P5: NH Beads O26 2-10˚C 20 tests 307-85681\nL165@P5: NH Beads O111 2-10˚C 20 tests 304-85691\nL166@P5: Fecal pretreatment reagent kit for Immunochromato\nL167@P5: “POTAT”\nL168@P5: • This kit inhibits non-specific reactions caused by poultry feces-derived\nL169@P5: materials, minimizing the number of false positives.\nL170@P5: • Tests can be conducted directly on fecal sample. Enrichment is not\nL171@P5: required.\nL172@P5: • This kit enables on-site testing in farms and poultry meat processing\nL173@P5: facilites.\nL174@P5: • The protocol is easy to perform. No special equipment is required.\nL175@P5: • Only 1 hour from sample collection to results.\nL176@P5: POTAT\nL177@P5: Product Storage Package Size Wako Cat. No.\nL178@P5: \"POTAT\" Fecal pretreatment reagent kit for Immunochromato 2-10˚C 20 tests 387-05481\nL179@P5: Apply the supernatant to\nL180@P5: the immunochromatography device\nL181@P5: Sample collection\nL182@P5: (using the scoop\nL183@P5: attached to the lid\nL184@P5: of tube containing\nL185@P5: dilution buffer)\nL186@P5: Dilute the sample\nL187@P5: and\nL188@P5: leave to sediment\nL189@P5: (≥10 minutes)\nL190@P5: Boil the\nL191@P5: supernatant for\nL192@P5: 10 minutes\nL193@P5: Cooling to ambient\nL194@P5: temperature\nL195@P5: Add additive in\nL196@P5: drops to solution\nL197@P5: Invert to mix\nL198@P5: Leave to sediment\nL199@P5: (≥10 minutes)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCrystal Sea® Marinemix: Marine Salt for Aquatics | MEI (https://meisalt.com/crystal-sea-marinemix/)\nciteturn30view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://meisalt.com/crystal-sea-marinemix/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 63\nL0: Argentina | Austria | Belize | Canada | Dominican Republic | Egypt | European Union | Great Britain | Guatemala | Guyana | Hong Kong | India | Japan | Malaysia | Mexico | New Zealand | Norway | Peru | South Korea | Thailand | Trinidad + Tobago | UAE\nL1: \nL2:   * 【0†Home】\nL3:   * 【1†About】\nL4:   * 【2†The MEI Benefit】\nL5:   * 【3†Products】\nL6:   * 【4†Crystal Sea^{®} In Use】\nL7: \nL8:   * 【0†Home】\nL9:   * 【1†About】\nL10:   * 【2†The MEI Benefit】\nL11:   * 【3†Products】\nL12:   * 【4†Crystal Sea^{®} In Use】\nL13: \nL14: ###### MENU\nL15: \nL16: 【5†contact us】\nL17: \nL18: 【6†Image】\nL19: # Crystal Sea^{®} Marinemix: Marine Salt for Commercial Aquatics\nL20: \nL21: One Marinemix Does it All\nL22: \nL23: Crystal Sea^{®} Marinemix provides complete duplication of natural sea water’s major, minor, and trace elements and is suitable and safe for all forms of marine life. Our Marinemix is scientifically blended, ensuring a consistent balance of all anhydrous ingredients, and clears within minutes!\nL24: Crystal Sea^{®} does not include any unnecessary additives or organics, including ammonia, nitrate, phosphate, silicate or E.D.T.A, and no additional trace elements or use of additional salts is needed.\nL25: \nL26: Sodium thiosulfate is included in each batch to ensure instant removal of chlorine from tap water.\nL27: \nL28: For more information on pricing and how to procure our products, 【5†contact us today.】\nL29: \nL30: 【7†Image: MEI_Product_Shot_1】\nL31: \nL32: 【8†Image: MEI_Product_Shot_3】\nL33: \nL34: 【9†Image: raw salt】\nL35: \nL36: 【10†Image: MEI_Product_Shot_8】\nL37: 【11†Image: MEI_Product_Shot_11】\nL38: \nL39: 【12†View Next Product:Crystal Sea^{®} Bioassay Laboratory Formula Marinemix】\nL40: ## Get In Touch\nL41: \nL42: #### We’d like to keep in touch with you!\nL43: \nL44: Contact us to learn more about our products!\nL45: \nL46: 【5†contact us】\nL47: \nL48: 【13†Image】\nL49: \nL50: ### Contact Us\nL51: \nL52: #### 【0†Marine Enterprises International】\nL53: \nL54:   * (410) 682-5303 | 800-200-SALT\nL55:   * (410) 687-2562\nL56:   * 8800 A Kelso Drive | Baltimore, MD 21221\nL57: \nL58:   * (410) 682-5303\nL59:   * 800-200-SALT\nL60:   * (410) 687-2562\nL61:   * 8800 A Kelso Drive | Baltimore, MD 21221\nL62: ### Copyright © 2026 Marine Enterprises International, LLC All Rights Reserved | 【14†LEGAL / TERMS OF SALE / CODE OF CONDUCT】\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nOxoid™ Peptonised Milk 250g | Request for Quote | Thermo Scientific™ | thermofisher.com (https://www.thermofisher.com/order/catalog/product/LP0032J)\nciteturn30view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.thermofisher.com/order/catalog/product