maaldrich/product/documents/338/431/c100pis.pdf\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 87\nL0@P0: Catalase\nL1@P0: from bovine liver\nL2@P0: Product Number C 100\nL3@P0: Product Description\nL4@P0: Enzyme Commission (EC) Number: 1.11.1.6\nL5@P0: CAS Number: 9001-05-2\nL6@P0: Molecular weight: 250 kDa1\nL7@P0: pI: 5.42\nL8@P0: Extinction Coefficient: E1% = 36.5 (276 nm)3\nL9@P0: Stoke's radius: 5.12 nm4\nL10@P0: Catalase from bovine liver is a tetramer consisting of\nL11@P0: 4 equal subunits with a molecular weight of 60 kDa\nL12@P0: each.5\nL13@P0:  Each subunit contains iron bound to a\nL14@P0: protoheme IX group. The enzyme also strongly binds\nL15@P0: NADP, which is in close proximity to the heme group\nL16@P0: (13.7 Å apart). 6\nL17@P0: Catalase catalyzes the following reaction:\nL18@P0: \nL19@P0: 2 H2O2→O2 + 2 H2O\nL20@P0: Catalase can also react with alkylhydrogen peroxides\nL21@P0: instead of H2O2, such as methylperoxide and\nL22@P0: ethylperoxide. In addition, many compounds can\nL23@P0: replace the second H2O2 molecule as the hydrogen\nL24@P0: donor, including methanol, ethanol, propanol, formate,\nL25@P0: and nitrate.7\nL26@P0: Catalase does not require any activators, but is\nL27@P0: inhibited by 3-amino-1-H-1,2,4 triazole, cyanide, azide,\nL28@P0: hydroxylamine, cyanogen bromide,\nL29@P0: 2-mercaptoethanol, dithiothreitol, dianisidine, and\nL30@P0: nitrate.8\nL31@P0:  Catalase is also inhibited by ascorbate and\nL32@P0: ascorbate with Cu2+. Incubation of catalase with\nL33@P0: ascorbate or ascorbate/Cu2+ results in degradation of\nL34@P0: the catalase molecule.9\nL35@P0:  Catalase activity is constant\nL36@P0: over the pH range of 4.0-8.5.10 Sigma determines the\nL37@P0: activity of this enzyme at pH 7.0.\nL38@P0: Precautions and Disclaimer\nL39@P0: For Laboratory Use Only. Not for drug, household or\nL40@P0: other uses.\nL41@P0: Preparation Instructions\nL42@P0: This product is offered as a catalase suspension in\nL43@P0: water containing 0.1% (w/v) thymol. In order to remove\nL44@P0: the thymol preservative, the catalase crystals may be\nL45@P0: pelleted by centrifugation, the supernatant discarded,\nL46@P0: the pellet resuspended in water, and then pelleted\nL47@P0: again. The pellet should then be resupended in 50 mM\nL48@P0: phosphate buffer, pH 7.0. Warming (30 °C) and slight\nL49@P0: agitation are required to reconstitute the catalase.\nL50@P0: Storage/Stability\nL51@P0: Solutions of catalase should not be frozen. Freezing\nL52@P0: stock solutions will cause a 50-70% loss in activity.\nL53@P0: References\nL54@P0: 1. Schroeder, W.A., et al., Some amino acid\nL55@P0: sequences in bovine liver catalase. Biochim.\nL56@P0: Biophys. Acta, 89, 47-65 (1964).\nL57@P0: 2. Samejima, T., et al., Dissociation of bovine liver\nL58@P0: catalase at low pH. J. Biochem. Japan, 51,\nL59@P0: 181-187 (1962).\nL60@P0: 3. Handbook of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology,\nL61@P0: 3rd Ed., Vol. II, Fasman, G.D., ed., CRC Press\nL62@P0: (Cleveland, OH: 1976), p. 403.\nL63@P0: 4. Journal of Chromatography, 152, 21 (1978).\nL64@P0: 5. Und, H., et al., Dissozition de Rinderleberkatalase\nL65@P0: in Ihre Untereinheiten. Eur. J. Biochem., 1, 400\nL66@P0: (1967).\nL67@P0: 6. Fita, I., and Rossmann, M.G., The NADPH binding\nL68@P0: site on beef liver catalase. Proc. Natl. Acad. Sci.\nL69@P0: USA, 82, 1604-1608 (1985).\nL70@P0: 7. Methods of Enzymatic Analysis, 3rd Ed., Vol. I,\nL71@P0: Bergmeyer, H.U., Ed., Academic Press (New\nL72@P0-1: York, NY: 1974), pp. 483-489. 8. The Enzyme Handbook, Vol. 7, Schomburg, D.,\nL73@P1: ed., Springer-Verlag (Berlin: 1993), EC 1.11.1.6,\nL74@P1: p. 2.\nL75@P1: 9. Orr, C.W., Studies on ascorbic acid II. Physical\nL76@P1: changes in catalase following incubation with\nL77@P1: ascorbate or ascorbate and copper (II).\nL78@P1: Biochemistry, 6, 3000-3006 (1967).\nL79@P1: 10. Chance, B., Effect of pH upon the reaction kinetics\nL80@P1: of the enzyme-substrate compounds of catalase.\nL81@P1: J. Biol. Chem., 194 471-481 (1952).\nL82@P1: TMG/JRC 11/03\nL83@P1: Sigma brand products are sold through Sigma-Aldrich, Inc.\nL84@P1: Sigma-Aldrich, Inc. warrants that its products conform to the information contained in this and other Sigma-Aldrich publications. Purchaser\nL85@P1: must determine the suitability of the product(s) for their particular use. Additional terms and conditions may apply. Please see reverse side of\nL86@P1: the invoice or packing slip.\n"
